  "each": "Fresh headless browser profile and distinct run id per case; slot runs and slot-free reviews. Lifecycle: write-task running, task written with its first read held in flight, criteria shown, real ledger error, recovered, task without criteria, then a second run opened after its task exists with its first read held.",
  "movement": "Change in the pipeline's height, which contains the criteria row; content loading above and the page scroll limit leave it alone.",
  "boundaries": [
    "A real ledger error keeps its existing auto-expanded panel, so that state grows by its error rows.",
    "A live run whose written task has no criteria releases the held row once its first read settles; nothing can tell earlier.",
    "A run opened after its task exists holds nothing, so its first criteria arrival behaves as before this change.",
    "Before recordings also show a resource-store restart notice from the archived base tree; it is not asserted."
  ],
  "limit": "Mounted Command Center over an isolated observed-WebSocket protocol fixture. No gateway, task writer, worker, native host or device is started."
